Q: How to call a statically linked Pascal function from a C main? A: <p><code>writeln</code> needs the Free Pascal RTL to be initialized, but your C <code>main</code> skips FPC's own startup. The segfault in <code>SYSTEM_$$_FINALIZEUNITS</code> happens because the finalizer is trying to clean up units that were never set up in the first place.</p>
<p>I'd fix this by manually calling the init/exit pair and linking the startup glue object <code>si_c.o</code> from your RTL directory:</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>/* main.c */
extern void fpc_initializeunits(void);
extern void fpc_do_exit(void);
void hello(void);

int main(void) {
    fpc_initializeunits();
    hello();
    fpc_do_exit();
    return 0;
}
</code></pre>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>fpc hello.pas
gcc main.c hello.o \
    /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/fpc/3.2.2/units/x86_64-linux/rtl/si_c.o \
    /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/fpc/3.2.2/units/x86_64-linux/rtl/system.o
</code></pre>
<p>Linking <code>system.o</code> alone isn't enough to handle the I/O, heap, and unit tables. So you need <code>si_c.o</code> to act as the bridge between glibc and the FPC runtime. Calling <code>fpc_initializeunits</code> ensures every unit's <code>initialization</code> block actually runs.</p>

Q: Get Observable value even if never emit A: <p>You have to use another stream that will emit immediately, and use <strong>RxJs combination operator</strong>. You can use <a href="https://www.learnrxjs.io/learn-rxjs/operators/combination/concat" rel="nofollow noreferrer">concat</a> (It will also preserve the order).</p>
<pre><code>ngOnInit(): void {

    concat(
      of(null),
      this.myservice.getFoo().pipe(tap((value) =&gt; console.log(value)))
    ).subscribe((data) =&gt; {
      console.log(data);
    });


    setTimeout(() =&gt; {
      this.myservice.init(true);
    }, 3000);
  }
</code></pre>

Q: Send calendar invite per email with java A: <p>There are actually a bunch of things wrong with your calendar code.</p>
<ol>
<li>For one you're missing an <code>ORGANIZER</code> and <code>ATTENDEE</code> (should be the recipient). You're also missing an <code>RSVP=TRUE</code>, which allows the attendee to respond first.</li>
<li>Your Mime message also is missing things like <code>method=REQUEST</code> matching the calendar's method (<code>METHOD:REQUEST</code>).</li>
<li>Calendar events being added automatically is not something you control btw; that's for the provider to manage (gmail in this case), probably per the user's settings.</li>
</ol>
<p>FYI: <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5546.html#section-3.2.2" rel="nofollow noreferrer">RFC 5546 §3.2.2</a> requires <code>ORGANIZER</code>, <code>ATTENDEE</code>, <code>DTSTAMP</code>, <code>DTSTART</code>, <code>SUMMARY</code>, and <code>UID</code> for a <code>VEVENT</code> request. <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6047.html#section-2.4" rel="nofollow noreferrer">RFC 6047 §2.4</a> requires the MIME <code>method</code> parameter to match the calendar’s <code>METHOD</code>.</p>
<p>You corrected usage would be something like:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>event.getProperties().add(
    new Organizer(URI.create(&quot;mailto:&quot; + fromMail))
);

for (Participant participant : session.getParticipants()) {
    Attendee attendee =
        new Attendee(URI.create(&quot;mailto:&quot; + participant.getEmail()));

    attendee.getParameters().add(Role.REQ_PARTICIPANT);
    attendee.getParameters().add(new Cn(participant.getName()));
    attendee.getParameters().add(PartStat.NEEDS_ACTION);
    attendee.getParameters().add(Rsvp.TRUE);

    event.getProperties().add(attendee);
}
</code></pre>
<p>And then <code>toMail</code> should match one of the attendees. Also, don't use <code>toString()</code> for calendar, but use iCal4j's <code>CalendarOutputter</code> for that.</p>
<p>Finally, the Mime message itself, fixed:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>MimeBodyPart invite = new MimeBodyPart();
invite.setContent(
    ics,
    &quot;text/calendar; charset=UTF-8; method=REQUEST&quot;
);
multipart.addBodyPart(invite);
</code></pre>
<hr />
<p>However, this is a lot of work for something that should be simple: just send an invitation to someone. There are open source projects that simplify this greatly. Simple Java Mail, for example makes your whole code as simple as:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>Email email = EmailBuilder.startingBlank()
    .from(&quot;Organizer&quot;, fromMail)
    .withRecipients(new RecipientBuilder()
        .withName(participantName)
        .withAddress(toMail)
        .withType(Message.RecipientType.TO)
        .build())
    .withSubject(subject)
    .withHTMLText(text)
    .withCalendarText(CalendarMethod.REQUEST, ics)
    .buildEmail();

Mailer mailer = MailerBuilder
    .withSMTPServer(smtpHost, smtpPort, smtpUser, smtpPassword)
    .withTransportStrategy(TransportStrategy.SMTP_TLS)
    .buildMailer();

mailer.sendMail(email);
</code></pre>
<p>No low level stuff like <code>Mime</code> and <code>VEvent</code>, and it has built in protection against injection attacks etc.</p>

Q: How to center text inside anchor tag A: <p>Another way to center text inside anchor tag:</p>
<pre><code>{   
    /* ... */
    display: inline-grid; /* or display: grid; */
    place-items: center;
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to make an animated menu icon show/hide menu A: <p>CSS (without changes)</p>
<pre><code>body {
  font-family: &quot;Lato&quot;, sans-serif;
}

.menuIcon {
  display: inline-block;
  cursor: pointer;
  float: left;
  margin: 1.3em 0 0 1em;
}

.menuBar1,
.menuBar2,
.menuBar3 {
  width: 2.5em;
  height: 0.4em;
  background-color: #000;
  margin: 0.3em;
  transition: 0.4s;
}

.change .menuBar1 {
  transform: translate(0, 0.7em) rotate(-45deg)
}

.change .menuBar2 {
  opacity: 0;
}

.change .menuBar3 {
  transform: translate(0, -0.7em) rotate(45deg)
}

.sidebar {
  height: 100%;
  width: 0;
  position: fixed;
  z-index: 1;
  top: 5em;
  left: 0;
  background-color: #111;
  overflow-x: hidden;
  transition: 0.5s;
  padding-top: 60px;
}

.sidebar a {
  padding: 8px 8px 8px 32px;
  ext-decoration: none;
  font-size: 25px;
  color: #818181;
  display: block;
  transition: 0.3s;
}

.sidebar a:hover {
  color: #f1f1f1;
}

.sidebar .closeBtn {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  right: 25px;
  font-size: 36px;
  margin-left: 50px;
}

.openBtn {
  font-size: 20px;
  cursor: pointer;
  background-color: #111;
  color: white;
  padding: 10px 15px;
  border: none;
}

.openBtn:hover {
  background-color: #444;
}

#main {
  transition: margin-left .5s;
  padding: 16px;
}

/* 
  On smaller screens, where height is less than 450px, 
  change the style of the sidenav 
  (less padding and a smaller font size) 
*/
@media screen and (max-height: 450px) {
  .sidebar {
    padding-top: 15px;
  }

  .sidebar a {
    font-size: 18px;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>It's all code in JS.</p>
<pre><code>function myFunction(x) {
  let menuIcon = document.getElementById(&quot;menuIcon&quot;) ;
  menuIcon.classList.toggle(&quot;change&quot;);
  if(menuIcon.classList.contains('change')){
    document.getElementById(&quot;mySidebar&quot;).style.width = &quot;250px&quot;;    
  }
  else {
    document.getElementById(&quot;mySidebar&quot;).style.width = 0;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<p>It's all code in HTML</p>
<pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
    &lt;html&gt;
    &lt;head&gt;
      &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1&quot;&gt;
     &lt;/head&gt;

    &lt;body&gt;

      &lt;div class=&quot;menuIcon&quot; id=&quot;menuIcon&quot; onclick=&quot;myFunction()&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;menuBar1&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;menuBar2&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;menuBar3&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt; 

      &lt;div id=&quot;mySidebar&quot; class=&quot;sidebar&quot;&gt;
        &lt;a href=&quot;javascript:void(0)&quot; class=&quot;closeBtn&quot; onclick=&quot;myFunction()&quot;&gt;×&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Services&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Clients&lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;a href=&quot;#&quot;&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;    

    &lt;/body&gt;
    &lt;/html&gt;
</code></pre>
